    "faq_Aw8WLn": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "item_GAXVJp": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "what safety guidelines should i follow when using the mōmi bottle?",
            "content": "<p>mōmi products certified to meet or exceed the U.S. regulatory requirements for infant safety. Even so, failure to follow the safety guidelines can shorten the life of the product, and can potentially result in a safety hazard. The soft silicone used in the mōmi nipple makes it more susceptible to damage when not used properly. Please read carefully and observe the safety instructions included with your product. These include the following:</p><ul><li>Do not use the nipple as a teething toy or pacifier. Using your mōmi nipple only for feeding will allow it to last much longer.</li><li>The soft silicone material is not designed to withstand excessive biting and gnawing.</li><li>Inspect the nipple and all bottle components before each use.</li><li>Discard immediately if the nipple has any signs of damage, puncture, cracking, or tearing.</li><li>Use only the mōmi cleaning tool in the nipple’s central duct, and never use a wire brush to clean the nipple. Wire brushes can damage the soft silicone interior of the nipple, causing a safety hazard.</li><li>Since silicone can break down over time, replace nipples after three months of regular use. </li></ul><p>Other important safety guidelines:</p><ul><li>Sterilize nipple and bottle components before first use. </li><li>Always check food temperature before feeding.</li><li>To avoid strangulation risk, do not attach cords, laces, or loose clothing to bottle or nipple.</li><li>Always discard any breast milk or formula that remains at the end of a feed.</li><li>Always use this product with adult supervision.</li><li>This is not a toy. Keep all components not in use out of the reach of children.</li><li>Do not allow children to play with small parts or walk/run while using bottles or nipples.</li><li>Remove the bottle from your baby’s mouth when the baby is not feeding.</li><li>Do not let baby take bottle to bed or self-feed for long periods of time.</li><li>Continuous and prolonged sipping of fluids will cause tooth decay.</li><li>Do not place in a heated oven.</li><li>Do not microwave. Liquid inside can heat unevenly or overheat and burn baby’s mouth even if outside of the bottle feels cool.</li><li>When warming breast milk or formula, stir thoroughly to eliminate hot or cold spots, test temperature frequently by placing a few drops on your tongue or back of your hand.</li><li>To prevent possible choking hazard, test strength of nipple regularly by pulling hard on it. Inspect carefully, especially when baby develops teeth, and replace nipple immediately if it shows any sign of wear or damage such as cracking or change of shape.</li><li>Do not leave nipple in direct sunlight or heat or leave in disinfectant (sterilizing solution) for longer than recommended as this may weaken the nipple.</li><li>To ensure the bottle functions correctly and to prevent leakage, make sure all the parts are correctly assembled, remove any debris or residue that may collect around the rim of the bottle before assembly and avoid over-tightening the collar.</li><li>Contact your physician should you have any feeding problems or questions.</li></ul><p><a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0539/1004/4843/files/2.0_product_safety_brochure-English_Spanish.pdf?v=1727180102\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0539/1004/4843/files/2.0_product_safety_brochure-English_Spanish.pdf?v=1727180102\">Check out our full product review guide</a></p>",
            "custom-html": ""
          }
        },
        "item_anfBhK": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "is the mōmi bottle bpa-free?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, all of our products are BPA free.</p>",
            "custom-html": ""
          }
        },
        "item_6XCEag": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "does the mōmi bottle meet regulatory safety requirements?",
            "content": "<p>Our products are rigorously tested and independently certified for compliance with applicable safety regulations. This includes testing for physical/mechanical strength and chemical content.</p>",
            "custom-html": ""
          }
        },
        "item_VfEzQB": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "where are mōmi products manufactured?",
            "content": "<p>Our silicone nipples are made in Canada. Our plastic components are made in the U.S. and China by manufacturers with many years’ experience making baby bottles for some of America’s leading brands. Our glass bottles are made with borosilicate glass by a leading Chinese manufacturer, and have been certified to be lead-free (including the ink) and compliant with U.S. regulatory standards.</p>",
            "custom-html": ""
          }
        },
        "item_ECFQpK": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "what if my mōmi nipple is beginning to split or crack?",
            "content": "<p>Discontinue use immediately and replace with a new nipple.<br/><br/>All silicone products wear out over time. Biting and gnawing, exposure to UV from sunlight or sterilizers, and use of abrasive cleaners are just a few factors that can accelerate the aging of the mōmi nipple. The mōmi nipple is designed to last at least three months under normal use conditions.<br/><br/>If you believe your mōmi nipple has a manufacturing defect, contact us by email at <a href=\"mailto:care@momi.baby\" title=\"mailto:care@momi.baby\">care@momi.baby</a>, by voicemail or text to 980-400-6455, or by chat here on our website. If possible, send us a photo of what you’re seeing.<br/></p>",
            "custom-html": ""
          }
        },
        "item_q6hit4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "what if my baby’s chewing has begun to cut into the nipple?",
            "content": "<p>Discontinue use immediately and replace with a new nipple.</p>",
            "custom-html": ""
          }
        },
        "item_DqfAkJ": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "what if my mōmi nipple has a small bubble in the tip?",
            "content": "<p>Small bubbles within the solid silicone tip can occur normally in the manufacturing process, and are not a defect. Large bubbles, particularly those that connect with the milk duct, may indicate a manufacturing defect.</p><p>If you believe your mōmi nipple has a manufacturing defect, contact us by email at <a href=\"mailto:care@momi.baby\" title=\"mailto:care@momi.baby\">care@momi.baby</a>, by voicemail or text to 980-400-6455, or by chat here on our website. If possible, send us a photo of what you’re seeing.</p>",
            "custom-html": ""
          }
        },
        "item_xaPF8J": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "how often should i replace the mōmi nipple?",
            "content": "<p>We recommend replacing the mōmi nipple after three months of normal use. If a baby with teeth has chewed or gnawed on the nipple excessively, or if the nipple has been exposed to excessive UV radiation such as from sunlight or a sterilizer, more frequent replacement may be necessary.</p>",
            "custom-html": ""
          }
        }
      },
