    "faq_r7KfHN": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "item_BVz8dr": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "what’s new about the bottle?",
            "content": "<p> </p>",
            "custom-html": "<p>The new nipple is longer, and shaped optimally to help babies to achieve a healthy, natural latch.  It’s also now soft and stretchy throughout, not just in the tip. We also redesigned the collar and clear cap to fit the new nipple.  (See more below on compatibility.)</p><br>\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0539/1004/4843/files/image_124.png?v=1726123882\">"
          }
        },
        "item_WtjFtB": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "i have original mōmi bottles. can i use them with the new nipples?",
            "content": "<p>Yes! Our glass and plastic bottles are both compatible with the new babypace® 2 nipple, used alongside gen 2 collars and clear nipple caps.  <a href=\"/products/momi-byob-replacement\" title=\"mōmi gen 2 replacement set\">The babypace® 2 replacement set</a>, which includes the new nipple, collar, and cap, is a great way to use your gen 1 bottles with the new nipple design.</p>",
            "custom-html": ""
          }
        },
        "item_QqiMtt": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "what’s compatible?",
            "content": "<p> </p>",
            "custom-html": "<ul>\n<li>bottles:  all of our bottles are compatible with both gen 1 and gen 2.</li>\n<li>cleaning tools:  gen 1 and gen 2 use the same cleaning tool.</li>\nwhat’s not compatible?\n<li>nipples + collars + clear nipple caps.  These are not interchangeable between generations.  Attempting to mix these parts between generations can cause problems - like leaks, poor fit, or caps becoming stuck to collars.  Think of the nipple + collar + cap as a complete set that can’t be mixed and matched between the two generations.</li>\nhow do I tell them apart?\n<li>nipples:  The babypace® 2 nipple is taller and has a large numerical flow rate indicator molded into the base.  The Gen 1 nipple is shorter and has a small “s”, “m” , or “f” flow rate indicator molded into the base.<br><br>\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0539/1004/4843/files/4_img.png?v=1727421148\"><br>\n</li> \n\n<li>caps:  The gen 2 clear nipple cap is taller than the gen 1, to fit the taller nipple. [include side by side photos]</li>\n<li>collars:  This is the tricky one. There are three ways to tell them apart.\n<ul class=\"sublistbullte\">\n<li>\nThe gen 1 collar has a “dimple” in the top surface (concealed by the nipple when it’s attached).  The gen 2 collar doesn’t have this dimple.<br><br>\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0539/1004/4843/files/2_img.png?v=1727421147\">\n</li>\n<li>The notches on the bottom surface of gen 1 are rectangular and spaced further apart than the rounded notches of the gen 2 collar.<br><br>\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0539/1004/4843/files/3_img.png?v=1727421147\"><br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n</li>\n<li>The gen 1 collar has an extra ridge inside where it makes contact with the nipple (highlighted by the arrow in the photo).</li>\n<li>The Gen 2 collar doesn’t have that ridge.<br><br>\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0539/1004/4843/files/1_img.png?v=1727421147\">\n</li>\n</ul>"
          }
        }
